EPSG Geodetic Parameter Dataset
-------------------------------
GeoFrame embeds coordinate reference system definitions and coordinate operation parameters
derived from the EPSG Geodetic Parameter Dataset, which is the property of the International
Association of Oil & Gas Producers (IOGP). The data come from three places:

  * the `crs-definitions` crate (a dependency), generated from the EPSG registry;
  * the tables generated from the PROJ database (proj.db, pyproj 3.8 / PROJ 9.8) by
    test/reference/generate_crs_datum.py and committed under native/geoframe_core/src:
    crs_extra.bin (about 1 200 CRS definitions the crate lacks, as PROJJSON),
    datum_helmert.rs, datum_grids.rs, crs_names.rs and utm_crs.rs (datum operations by area of
    use, grid names, CRS names, UTM zones);
  * the PROJ database itself is part of PROJ, distributed under the MIT license by the PROJ
    contributors (https://proj.org), and contains the EPSG data.

The EPSG Dataset is made available under the EPSG terms of use
(https://epsg.org/terms-of-use.html): it may be used and redistributed free of charge as part of
software, provided its source is acknowledged and the data are not presented as an official
version. The data are provided "as is" without warranty of any kind; IOGP and the other
contributors accept no liability for their use. Use the EPSG registry (https://epsg.org) for the
authoritative definitions.
